draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122988","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122988","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122988.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122988.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- If the `Align Y` flag is enabled, all `Angle` settings are ignored.\r\n- Orbit velocity is not accounted for during `Align Y` calculations.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nMany times I (and others I have talked with) have been annoyed by the `Align Y` flag forcing one specific angle. I made this small PR to fix that issue, along with a similar issue with orbit velocity.\r\n\r\nI was thinking of splitting this into two PRs, but I felt like they were closely enough related that splitting them would be unhelpful.\r\n\r\n### Additional Work\r\n\r\n- The new variable on line 899 could probably be moved somewhere else or perhaps somehow removed.\r\n- If the particles have orbit velocity, the first frame a particle spawns the orbit is not calculated and thus, flashes the angle for one frame.\r\n- The orbit velocity angle calculations could be simplified to use more direct math rather than calculating the difference in positions. This would also fix the above issue.\r\n- The bottom two modified lines could be wrapped in an if statement to skip performing unnecessary math.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122988/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122988/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}